## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to optimize prompts for cost and speed, exercising token budgeting and simple NLP heuristics in prompt engineering.

## Key Concepts
- Token counting and budgets
- Intent preservation
- Heuristic trimming

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal compress
function compress(p){
  // naive: drop time qualifiers and rephrase
  let q = p
    .replace(/in the last \d+ months?/i, "")
    .replace(/and export\s+their\s+emails\s+to\s+a\s+CSV\s+file/gi, "export emails to CSV");
  return q.trim();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate compression ratio vs fidelity?
- How would you handle languages other than English?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical routing logic for multi-tenant LLM services under latency and safety constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant SLAs and data locality
- Model-version routing (fast/balanced/safety) and drift audits
- Lightweight policy engine and simple telemetry

